    "title": "Emmy Noether: Modern LaTeX Working Corpus and Multilingual Translation Drafts (v26/R819 Paper 20 Source Integration)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21320035",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-12",
    "description": "<p>This is the reader-facing Emmy Noether working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. This version fronts <code>00_Noether_German_Cumulative_Working_SourceControl_v26_R819integrated_20260712.pdf</code>, a 466-page German working reader. The matching TeX, source witnesses, audit ledgers, integration diff, render checks, prior v26 head, and build logs are grouped in <code>07_Noether_Current_German_SourceControl_v26_R819integrated_20260712.zip</code>.</p><p><strong>What changed:</strong> the published v26 German base now incorporates the R818 and R819 direct source sweeps of Paper 20, <em>Absolute Irreduzibilitaet in einem beliebigen Grundkoerper</em>. R818 records 17 source-backed corrections across printed pages 26-32, including display-number placement, punctuation and footnote-mark placement, relocation of footnote 8, and the substantive correction <code>U_i</code> to <code>U_lambda</code>. R819 records eight further emphasis and punctuation corrections across printed pages 31-33. No OCR text was promoted. An integration check confirms that every byte outside Paper 20 is preserved from v26 and that the integrated Paper 20 exactly matches the sealed R819 text.</p><p><strong>Status caveat:</strong> this is a serious source-repair and translation working corpus, not a critical edition, author-wide source-faithfulness certification, paper-by-paper certification, complete multilingual synchronization, or publication-grade proofreading. The retained English and multilingual readers predate some German repairs. Inherited terms such as <code>COMPLETE</code>, <code>closure</code>, or <code>closed</code> refer only to bounded local tasks.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> corrections, source comparisons, LaTeX fixes, and translation improvements can be suggested via issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
